Tony wrote in Tony says hey David which  drugs do you think should be legalized  or decriminalized so number one it's  good that you're making the distinction  between legalized and decriminalized  because legalization and  decriminalization are very different  things and also it's important to  distinguish between trafficking and  personal use okay so let's go in order  all drug use and drug possession for  personal amounts should be  decriminalized period legalization  absolutely for marijuana and for other  drugs I'm open to discussion you look I  believe it's Denver that's testing  legalizing mushrooms as an example I  have less of a fixed opinion about the  legalization of some drugs  I've not seen good reasons to legalize  recreational cocaine or heroin for  example I'm very clear that possessing  cocaine or heroin for personal use  should not be a crime using cocaine or  heroin should not be a crime but the  recreational legalization of cocaine and  heroin I just I've not seen a good  argument for that and I'm willing to  have my mind change now this gets us to  a really important element of this  debate that a lot of people miss a lot  of people seem not to understand that  when you talk about legalization or  decriminalization of any drug you're not  talking about it being legal to be  trafficking in those drugs ten pounds of  marijuana or a kilo of coke or whatever  whether you decriminalize or legalize  that is likely still going to be  criminal and when you think about it  alcohol is legal recreational  e-cigarettes are legal recreationally it  is still against the law to traffic and  alcohol or cigarettes without doing it  you know on the record as a business in  the way that the the guidelines say that  you should you can have that debate and  I'm glad to have it but it's important  to understand and I think that there are  a lot of bad faith actors on the anti  decriminalization anti  legalization tends to be the political  right in the United States who either  are misunderstanding or they are  deliberately conflating the  decriminalization or legalization of the  trafficking of drugs versus legalization  and decriminalization of amounts for  personal use and these are very very  different conversations so my question  to you today is what is the strongest  argument for recreational legalization  of drugs like cocaine and heroin I am a  hundred and ten percent on board with  marijuana I would sooner make cigarettes  illegal then say that marijuana should  remain criminal for use and possession  but I have not seen a good case made for  why there should be recreationally legal  cocaine or heroin but if you've got a  good argument to make along those lines  by all means get in touch and then we  can talk about it
 

